1
00:00:01,459 --> 00:00:06,965
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,593
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,224
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:17,809
Gavin!

6
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:18,685
[growls]

7
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:19,769
Do you know, the one I was chasing?

8
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:21,020
That's someone I chat with.

9
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:23,440
I really wanted to
meet her IRL.

10
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:24,482
Siony: A real zombie, Sir!

11
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:26,568
It bites, Sir!

12
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:27,986
[screaming & panicking]

13
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:29,571
Karla: Gavin!

14
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:31,781
Gavin! Help me!

15
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:33,450
Elias: I said stop!

16
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,910
[growling & screaming]

17
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:36,703
Shugo: Sir, Sir, Sir!

18
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:37,454
Elias: Aargh!

19
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:38,538
Ahh, let go of me!

20
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,290
[screaming]

21
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:42,125
Baker, Baker!

22
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:43,877
I'm Atoy.

23
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,420
I'm Atoy, I'm Master Cutter!

24
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:46,463
What did they do to you?!

25
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:47,922
Dickson!

26
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:49,007
Baker escaped.

27
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,133
What are you talking about?

28
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:51,134
The Baker is dead.

29
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:54,012
Goon 1: He escaped while
being transported.

30
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:55,263
Atoy: Where are you?
What's the location?

31
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:56,264
58…

32
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:59,350
North, 12--

33
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:00,018
Washer.

34
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:00,894
Washer?

35
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:01,728
What's the washer?!

36
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:02,437
Baker--

37
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,271
Medic! Medic!

38
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:05,815
When are you really going
to meet her, bro?

39
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:07,108
Rommel: We already met.

40
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:09,444
Rommel: She was here at the run earlier.

41
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:11,154
Let’s go on a double date with Karla.

42
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:12,155
O-- of course.

43
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:13,948
Audrey: Ah, there's-- there's a woman.

44
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:15,200
There's-- she has a hair clip.

45
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:15,909
Jona: Oh no. Hair clip?

46
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:16,951
Atoy: Dickson Tonido.

47
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,203
That's the name of the…

48
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:19,621
zombie who attacked me.

49
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:20,872
He's The Baker.

50
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:21,748
Sir?

51
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:23,249
It looks like he was experimented on.

52
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:25,251
Jesabel: I knew it!

53
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,378
Are you flirting with each other?!

54
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,006
Can you not? Read the room!

55
00:01:30,089 --> 00:01:32,342
121, 2, 39, East.

56
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:34,010
Did he say anything else?

57
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:35,386
Washer.

58
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:37,639
Jesabel: Ah, Washer.

59
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:38,431
Washer.

60
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:40,517
Obviously, these are coordinates.

61
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,559
This will point us directly

62
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:43,228
to the location of the Washer.

63
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:44,604
Let's focus on this.

64
00:01:44,687 --> 00:01:45,939
[music continues]

65
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:46,815
Mmm-hmm.

66
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:49,317
[music swells]

67
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:55,240
[laughing]
[lively chatter]

68
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:56,783
Oh, you.

69
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:58,451
That's just how it is.

70
00:01:58,535 --> 00:01:59,577
[overlapping chatter]

71
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:01,746
Right? Yes.

72
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,081
[lively chatter]

73
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,249
[laughing]

74
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:05,667
He was even drooling like that,

75
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:06,251
aargh, aargh!

76
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,794
So, I kicked him like that!

77
00:02:07,877 --> 00:02:09,129
[laughs]

78
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:09,963
And then, he got mad at him!

79
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:10,964
So, he got chased instead!

80
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:11,673
[laughs]

81
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:12,674
Really?

82
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:13,842
Scary!

83
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,511
Oh, Uncle, it was very scary.

84
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:17,804
Too bad you didn't see it.

85
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:18,847
Emerson: Yes, indeed.

86
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,515
I punched him, it had no effect.

87
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,851
Well, where could that have come from?

88
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:26,980
Didn't you say Velma was bitten?

89
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:28,314
How is she now?

90
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:28,940
Oh?

91
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:30,567
You know, I just noticed.

92
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:32,068
She doesn't leave her house.

93
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:33,945
Paldo: What could have happened to her?

94
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:36,072
Well, wait, wait.

95
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:36,990
Mmm?

96
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:39,367
When you get bitten by a zombie…

97
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,411
well, you become a zombie too!

98
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:43,163
I'm absolutely sure,

99
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,122
her appearance is already changing.

100
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:44,831
She’s doing this already.

101
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:45,748
Karla: Oh no.

102
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:46,416
[squeals]

103
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:47,542
[clamoring]

104
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:48,710
Ow, ow!

105
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:52,463
So, so what? Zombie-like?

106
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:53,214
Oh my, Uncle!

107
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,841
You should give us garlic!

108
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:57,010
We need to put some in the houses!

109
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:58,928
- Garlic? Is it garlic?
- No, My Loves, you see,

110
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:00,471
Garlic doesn't work on it.

111
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,765
Huh? Well, what do we do?!

112
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:05,560
Ah, well then just kiss me.

113
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:06,311
Oh, oh.

114
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:07,854
[teasing & laughing]

115
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:09,564
[lively chatter]

116
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:11,024
Sorry! Sorry, My Loves.

117
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:12,859
[overlapping chatter]
Kiss him, kiss him, kiss him!

118
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:14,360
Paldo! Kiss him!

119
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:16,988
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪
[theme music playing]

120
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:20,533
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

121
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:24,621
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

122
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:26,581
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

123
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:27,999
♪ The hole in my polo

124
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:30,460
that's right under the armpit ♪

125
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:32,253
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

126
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:34,172
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

127
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:36,007
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

128
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:40,553
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

129
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:41,846
[gunshots]

130
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,264
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

131
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,558
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

132
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:47,310
[music swells]

133
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:51,231
[music fades]

134
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:55,610
Janine, for Christmas…

135
00:03:56,527 --> 00:04:00,114
can we give clothes and toys to…

136
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:01,658
orphanages?

137
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:05,370
It doesb’t have to be the
one we came from.

138
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,041
Big Sis Ame said there are
other orphanages.

139
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,751
Shh!

140
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,254
Don't be noisy.

141
00:04:15,004 --> 00:04:17,674
Someone might hear you,
there are people here.

142
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:19,592
Ibyang: Huh? Why?

143
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,137
But then…

144
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:26,140
Past is past, this is our new life.

145
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:30,228
Janine, are you still sad that I'm

146
00:04:30,311 --> 00:04:33,231
Mommy and Tatoy's real child?

147
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:34,899
Ibyang: They adopted you.

148
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,401
So that means

149
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:40,029
we're both real children now!

150
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:41,114
You're a Padua already.

151
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,075
I know.

152
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:46,619
But anyway, we won't tell that story

153
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:47,870
to everyone. Okay?

154
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:50,331
The only thing they
need to know…

155
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:53,126
is that you're Ibyang Thread,

156
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:55,253
and I'm Janine Needle.

157
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:57,547
Team Padua for the win!

158
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:00,008
[clapping]

159
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:03,386
Eyy! Team Padua!

160
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:05,513
[heavy music playing]

161
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:07,015
Let's make more beats.

162
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:10,184
That's the date. November 14, 2026.

163
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:11,978
On that day,

164
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:15,440
this Washer will come to this place

165
00:05:16,065 --> 00:05:18,109
and they'll have a transaction there.

166
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:21,446
[pensive music playing]

167
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:22,530
[grunts]

168
00:05:22,613 --> 00:05:23,698
I'll make it up to you, Sir.

169
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:27,744
I'll get stronger so I can assist
you on the mission.

170
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:30,663
I trust you, Uno.

171
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:41,799
[music swells]

172
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:42,633
[clamoring]

173
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:43,384
Hurry up, T-Bak!

174
00:05:43,468 --> 00:05:45,386
Hurry up!
[clamoring]

175
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,888
Maybe he's about to come out.

176
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,347
[clamoring]

177
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,640
You're taking so long, you know.

178
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,225
[clamoring]

179
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:52,727
Paldo: There, let's see.

180
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:55,855
[anxious music playing]

181
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:57,190
[squeals]

182
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:58,941
Wait-- wait, wait.

183
00:05:59,025 --> 00:05:59,984
What I mean is maybe--

184
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:02,070
Did you already ask Father Peping

185
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:03,571
to bless this house?

186
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:07,158
But Velma isn't possessed!

187
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:08,868
Well, it's the same thing.

188
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:11,037
Possessed, zombie.

189
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:13,164
It's good to pray for her!

190
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:14,665
But don't you pity her?

191
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,501
How long will she be locked up in there?

192
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,420
Until she gets better!

193
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:23,299
And besides, just think about this, Karla.

194
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:25,551
If she gets loose,

195
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:27,053
she could bite all of us!

196
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:27,845
[gasps & squeals]

197
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,597
And I can't become a zombie, you know!

198
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,473
Why?!

199
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:31,974
Well, I'm missing some teeth.

200
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:33,184
[mysterious music playing]

201
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:35,686
So noisy.

202
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:41,359
[music swells]

203
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:44,320
What are you doing here?!

204
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,786
[gasps & squeals]

205
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:55,206
[frantic music playing]

206
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:57,667
[screaming & panicking]

207
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:58,251
Paldo: Hey!

208
00:06:58,334 --> 00:06:59,836
[clamoring & panicking]

209
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:01,420
Paldo: What are you doing here?!

210
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:02,421
You were inside, right?!

211
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:04,841
Quiet!

212
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,301
You're all so overdramatic!

213
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:09,554
I didn't become a zombie!

214
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:13,182
I have a stiff neck, that's why
my neck hurts!

215
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:15,226
[pleasant music playing]

216
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:17,854
And why are you all here?

217
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,689
Can you all get lost?!

218
00:07:19,772 --> 00:07:21,274
I want to rest!

219
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:22,275
What are you doing at my gate?

220
00:07:22,358 --> 00:07:23,151
You're not leaving, huh?!

221
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:24,610
[growling]

222
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:27,196
[screaming & panicking]

223
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:29,115
[frantic music playing]
[growling]

224
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:30,616
[screaming & panicking]

225
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,535
[indistinct chattering]

226
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:33,703
These people.

227
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:38,124
[metal clanging]

228
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:40,710
[gate lock clicks]

229
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:43,379
[laughs]

230
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,714
But she really looks like a zombie, right?

231
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:46,716
Yes. That's why I got nervous.

232
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:47,592
Wait, um…

233
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:48,259
[music fades]

234
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:50,553
What's the news about…

235
00:07:50,636 --> 00:07:51,637
um, the…

236
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,389
what Miss Siony asked us to do,

237
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:55,516
the one she brought, remember, the…

238
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,351
The problem about the mistress

239
00:07:57,435 --> 00:08:00,229
of her cousin's husband.

240
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:01,105
What's the news on that?

241
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,815
I'll take care of it, Emerson.

242
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:06,194
I know where…

243
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:08,488
Elvis and Rochelle hang out.

244
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:10,740
You'll see, later we'll have evidence.

245
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:11,574
I'll take care of it.

246
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,493
[sneaky music playing]

247
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:18,039
It looks like he was tortured, Sir.

248
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:20,374
Aside from having several broken ribs,

249
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:23,169
there's bleeding in some
of his internal organs,

250
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,464
and he has hypodermic needle punctures

251
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:28,758
in different parts of his neck and arms.

252
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,885
What were…

253
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:32,553
injected into him?

254
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,764
I've already sent the sample
to the lab, Sir.

255
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:37,517
But they said they can't identify it.

256
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,228
[suspicious music playing]

257
00:08:40,311 --> 00:08:41,437
Thank you, Nurse.

258
00:08:43,272 --> 00:08:45,733
[music continues]

259
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:51,864
Janine: Hi, guys! Sorry I'm late.

260
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,282
Sorry, I'm late.

261
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,575
You're not late, Janine. No.

262
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,036
Wait, Janine.

263
00:08:57,828 --> 00:08:58,871
Didn't you say

264
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,373
you and Ibyang are fraternal twins?

265
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,083
Um…

266
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,961
Ah, yes. Why?

267
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:07,547
How did that happen? You're adopted.

268
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:10,341
[heavy music playing]

269
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:11,092
Huh?

270
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:14,178
Why are you lying, Janine?

271
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,973
Leighton: So, you lied to us.

272
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:18,849
You're really not Ibyang's sister.

273
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,601
[music continues]

274
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:23,604
Liar liar, pants on fire.

275
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:26,399
[laughing]

276
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:28,651
Adopted.

277
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,361
[music intensifies]

278
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:31,279
Wait--

279
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:34,031
[music continues]

280
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:36,200
Hmm! Janine, Janine!

281
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,286
Hmm, don't cry anymore.

282
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:40,371
Don't cry anymore. Are you okay?

283
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:40,997
No!

284
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,957
Don't cry anymore.

285
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,500
How did they find out?

286
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:46,460
Who told them?

287
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:48,379
I don't know. I'm not sure.

288
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:51,591
Who?

289
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:57,013
[music intensifies]

290
00:10:00,474 --> 00:10:02,310
I saw Leighton talking to someone earlier.

291
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:07,231
[suspicious music playing]

292
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:09,483
Well-- who?

293
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:11,110
Ibyang!

294
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:14,363
[tense music playing]

295
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:25,124
Wanbol, I have a question.

296
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:26,542
What?

297
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,336
[muffled chattering in the distance]

298
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,545
Ah, never mind.

299
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:30,963
What is it?

300
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,673
[playful music playing]

301
00:10:33,215 --> 00:10:34,467
Well…

302
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:35,760
[music continues]

303
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,471
We didn't pick up any fish.

304
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:40,556
Why do you still smell like fish?

305
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,265
Well, sorry.

306
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:44,185
Ah, so-- sorry, sorry, sorry!

307
00:10:44,268 --> 00:10:46,020
That's not what I meant.

308
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,480
It's not bad.

309
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:51,984
It's just that our classmates

310
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,903
are avoiding you.

311
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,780
[soft drama music playing]

312
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:58,658
I have an idea! Here, look, oh.

313
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:03,412
Where is it? There, this.

314
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,748
Oh, ta-da!

315
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,709
My mama uses this on me

316
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:09,960
after I take a bath.

317
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:12,630
Mmm. You can have that.

318
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:15,591
[light music playing]

319
00:11:15,674 --> 00:11:16,217
It smells so nice!

320
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:19,303
Oh, right?

321
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:21,472
Thank you, Ibyang!

322
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:26,394
Ah, Wanbol…

323
00:11:27,603 --> 00:11:28,854
I have a question.

324
00:11:29,438 --> 00:11:31,232
Why do you always smell like fish?

325
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:38,697
[rousing music playing]

326
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:39,448
Hello, Uno?

327
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,201
Yes, it really looks like The Baker

328
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:43,285
was experimented on.

329
00:11:44,912 --> 00:11:46,997
Nothing, even the doctors can't trace it,

330
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:49,166
they can't figure out what drugs

331
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:51,043
were pumped into him.

332
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:52,795
[sneaky music playing]

333
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:56,757
[camera shutter snapping]

334
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:57,800
[music continues]

335
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,970
[clicking]

336
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:02,513
[music continues]

337
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:09,145
I'll go home first,

338
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:11,063
so I can figure out our plan

339
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,189
for The Washer.

340
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:14,483
[music continues]

341
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,526
Gotcha.

342
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,653
Oh, okay. Hey!

343
00:12:18,612 --> 00:12:19,447
[camera shutter snapping]

344
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:20,322
Hey, Miss.

345
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,367
[music continues]

346
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:28,914
Are you okay?

347
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:31,083
[music continues]

348
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,293
[blipping]

349
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:35,421
Mission accomplished.

350
00:12:37,339 --> 00:12:40,509
[tense music playing]

351
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:41,927
Ah, wait.

352
00:12:43,095 --> 00:12:44,472
I know you!

353
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:45,598
[soft rock music playing]

354
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:48,225
It feels like we've met somewhere before?

355
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:50,144
At the bar!

356
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:51,103
At the bar?

357
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,063
[music continues]

358
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:56,317
What’s your name again? Anton? Tony?

359
00:12:57,234 --> 00:12:57,985
Atoy.

360
00:12:58,068 --> 00:12:59,487
[music continues]

361
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:00,613
Georgia!

362
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:03,157
Georgia. Ah, okay.

363
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:04,617
Oh, okay.

364
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:08,162
Ah, sorry. Ah, right.

365
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:09,205
Maybe you just look alike.

366
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:10,831
Right. Maybe, maybe.

367
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:11,790
[chuckles softly]

368
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,584
- Ah, Georgia.
- You seem…

369
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:15,002
nicer than that guy.

370
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:17,171
Oh, okay.

371
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:20,674
Ah, are you okay now?

372
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:21,967
What is this?

373
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:25,137
My heels already got ruined,
from walking.

374
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:27,097
- Oh, is that so? Oh.
- Yes. Well--

375
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:30,684
I'm looking for a place to
rent, ah, a house.

376
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:32,478
- Atoy: Okay.
- There in Tabang Lupa.

377
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:33,270
Tabang Lupa?

378
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:36,440
Oh, I'm from Tabang Lupa.

379
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,235
- Really? Ah…
- Atoy: Yes.

380
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:40,653
Maybe you know of a…

381
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:41,862
place to rent?

382
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:43,781
It's close to where I teach.

383
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,617
Ah, I'm a pilates instructor.

384
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:48,494
- Pilates, yes.
- Yeah.

385
00:13:48,577 --> 00:13:50,871
The-- there are many rentals
in Tabang Lupa.

386
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,748
Nice ones too, surely,
and you'll be safe there.

387
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:54,833
Yes. Good luck with the search.

388
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,293
- Ah.
- Atoy: Okay.

389
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:58,337
[music continues]

390
00:13:58,420 --> 00:13:59,505
[music fades]

391
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:00,631
Ame: It's crazy, you know.

392
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:02,466
He suddenly appeared with…

393
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,634
a broken neck!

394
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:04,635
Oh my. It's because you all

395
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:05,844
love to meddle!

396
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,680
Good thing you didn't actually lock

397
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:09,056
Velma inside the house.

398
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:12,059
Oh, Miss Cita, you have a visitor.

399
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,227
Cita: Huh? What?

400
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:15,896
Oh, Cita.

401
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,273
Ah, Rudy.

402
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:18,524
Surprise!

403
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:19,441
[chuckles softly]

404
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:21,527
Ah, you mentioned to me that…

405
00:14:22,069 --> 00:14:24,738
you work here at the tailoring shop so…

406
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:27,741
I was planning to have
a matching set made.

407
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:30,911
Ahh. Ye-- ye-- yes, okay.

408
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:31,662
Let's go inside.

409
00:14:31,745 --> 00:14:32,246
Oh, by the way,

410
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:33,956
my son, Rommel.

411
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:35,249
Get your aunt’s blessing.

412
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:36,876
Hi, Rommel!

413
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:39,211
Papa has told me stories about you.

414
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:41,380
Oh my. I hope those were
good stories, ah.

415
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:42,214
Oh, my.

416
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:45,092
Not just good, he said
they’re unforgettable too.

417
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:46,343
Oh, hmm…

418
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:49,263
And I'm Ame, I'm an assistant

419
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:49,972
at the tailoring shop.

420
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,599
But I can also be a chaperone.

421
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:52,725
What? What did you say?

422
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:54,476
Ame: I said let's go inside,

423
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,811
because it's hot out here.

424
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:56,896
Ah, okay, okay. Ah…

425
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:58,856
Come, let's go inside.

426
00:14:58,939 --> 00:14:59,940
Ah okay, Pa, you go ahead.

427
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,567
I'll just go see Gavin.

428
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:04,403
- Huh? Gavin? Gavin Regalia?
- Thank you, guys. Thank you.

429
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:05,154
Yes.

430
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:06,655
Cita: Oh, you know him.

431
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:07,990
Small world.

432
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:10,284
He's the nephew of Atoy's wife.

433
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:13,120
My godson, he's also the owner
of the tailoring shop.

434
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:14,079
He'll be here later.

435
00:15:14,663 --> 00:15:15,372
Let's wait inside.

436
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:16,999
Oh, okay, okay.

437
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:18,083
Ah, let's go in.

438
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:20,461
Where did you come from?

439
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:26,425
[light music playing]

440
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:28,469
[suspicious music playing]

441
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,721
No freaking way! Gavin!

442
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:32,890
Oh my gosh! It's you!

443
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:34,808
Ah, wait.

444
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:37,102
You, ah, I'm upset with you.

445
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:38,979
I kept calling you at the run,

446
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,481
you didn't pay attention to me.

447
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:42,483
Chanty?

448
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,234
What are you doing here?

449
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,862
Ah, I accompanied my dad

450
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,197
to Baclaran church.

451
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,366
And then, I wandered around a bit

452
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,659
to look for the…

453
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,702
miraculous Saint Anthony?

454
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:55,621
And then, I see you here.

455
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:58,707
I didn't expect to see you here actually.

456
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:00,376
What? Are you from around here?

457
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:02,211
[somber music playing]

458
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:03,754
Chanty: What's wrong?

459
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:06,131
Aren't you happy or…

460
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,718
Gavin! Gavin!

461
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,846
Let's go. Coach is calling us.

462
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:14,390
Wait, bro. Why is it like that?

463
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:15,641
I'll explain to you later.

464
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:17,226
Come with me for now.

465
00:16:18,018 --> 00:16:20,020
Um, miss, we'll go ahead, okay.

466
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:21,814
Because we'll be late for the game.

467
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:23,941
Come on, let's go. Hurry up.

468
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:26,443
[suspicious music playing]

469
00:16:27,236 --> 00:16:28,320
What was that?

470
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:32,825
[music continues]

471
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:36,412
What?

472
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:39,832
Can't this get any blurrier, Paldo?

473
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:40,874
What is this? Were your hands clammy

474
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:42,042
when you took it?

475
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:42,918
Paldo: Well, sorry.

476
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:43,585
C’mon.

477
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:45,546
I got a nice shot.

478
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:47,256
It's-- it's clear, look.

479
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:48,298
Here, look. Look at this.

480
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:49,091
See?

481
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:51,343
Oh, this can be shown
to Miss Siony's niece.

482
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:52,136
Emerson: Okay, okay.

483
00:16:52,219 --> 00:16:53,053
Okay, that's fine.

484
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:54,096
Wait. Who is that?

485
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:55,764
Why?

486
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:57,433
Why?

487
00:16:57,516 --> 00:16:58,434
Look.

488
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,310
[sneaky music playing]

489
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:05,274
Atoy?

490
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:07,901
OMG!

491
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,778
[rock music playing]

492
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,155
Paldo: You're in trouble, Atoy.

493
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:13,782
[music continues]

494
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,664
Oh, see that?

495
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:22,124
[sneaky music playing]

496
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:24,043
The woman fell down the stairs,

497
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:25,461
I helped her.

498
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:26,920
Then the heel of her shoe broke.

499
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:28,547
I supported her.

500
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:29,506
Okay? Nothing, oh--

501
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:31,550
Nothing, we weren't even
supposed to be in that picture.

502
00:17:33,802 --> 00:17:35,471
Hmm. Are you sure? Is that all?

503
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,265
Yes. Why--

504
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:39,850
[music continues]

505
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,101
Why are you looking at me like that,

506
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:43,228
like the questions of people who judge--

507
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,063
Nothing!

508
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:44,855
No.

509
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:45,647
What-- what are you thinking?

510
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,775
Emerson: Nothing, no!

511
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:48,609
Come on, look.

512
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:50,319
I know you're loyal to Audrey.

513
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:51,236
Emerson: Oh, you.

514
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,529
You seem to be doubting me.

515
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:53,489
Emerson: No!

516
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:56,909
[laughs]

517
00:17:56,992 --> 00:17:58,327
Okay, okay, okay. Fine.

518
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,120
It's nothing. Well, anyway…

519
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:02,372
Just crop this picture.

520
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:03,415
Remove that.

521
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:04,458
You know how Miss Siony is.

522
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:05,375
If she sees that,

523
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:06,710
she might have other ideas.

524
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,837
Who knows what those people might think.

525
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:11,006
Sometimes their minds
are just malicious, you know.

526
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:13,342
I'll just crop it.
[suspicious music playing]

527
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:18,013
Janine: Ibyang!

528
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:20,182
[heavy music playing]

529
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:22,184
Why, Janine?

530
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,269
Why are you shouting? What happened?

531
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:27,106
Why did you say I'm adopted, huh?!

532
00:18:27,898 --> 00:18:29,650
Ibyang, you promised, didn't you?!

533
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:31,735
[music continues]

534
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:32,986
What is it, Ibyang?

535
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:34,905
Speak!

536
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,574
Why are you tattling that I'm adopted?!

537
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:39,618
But, Janine,

538
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:41,870
I don't know how they found out!

539
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:43,330
[music continues]

540
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:45,624
The whole dance club knows I'm adopted!

541
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:47,167
[music continues]

542
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:48,961
Wait. Wait, Janine.

543
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,879
Who told you that…

544
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,506
I'm the one tattling that you're adopted?

545
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,050
Who else?

546
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,218
Hailey!

547
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:59,513
Hailey is lying!

548
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:02,182
Don't deny it anymore, Ibyang!

549
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,308
Just admit it!

550
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,270
I was embarrassed because of you!

551
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:09,815
Put that away,
[music fades]

552
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:10,691
so there won't be any trouble.

553
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,151
[pensive music playing]

554
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:13,110
It looks--

555
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:16,113
It's obvious that it was cropped.

556
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:16,697
Not really. Well, rather than--

557
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:17,865
Someone will see, um--

558
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:19,491
Easy. Here it is.

559
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:20,993
How did it happen that suddenly,

560
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:22,244
there was a picture like that?

561
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:22,953
Okay, okay.

562
00:19:23,036 --> 00:19:24,037
There, there, there, here it is, oh.

563
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:24,663
Here, it's gone.

564
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:26,248
Perfectly safe now. Okay, huh.

565
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:27,791
- Okay. That's good.
- Emerson: There.

566
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,375
Oh, let's go.

567
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,710
Oh, this is the…

568
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:30,836
evidence, okay.

569
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:32,754
I'm going to keep this in the shop.

570
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:33,839
Emerson: Oh, all right.

571
00:19:33,922 --> 00:19:36,425
Ah, I can report to Miss Siony now.

572
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:38,302
We'll earn quite a bit from this, 'Toy.

573
00:19:38,385 --> 00:19:39,636
[cackles]

574
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:40,262
[door lock clicks]

575
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,806
Hey. Sorry, sorry…

576
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:43,891
Emerson, sorry.

577
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:45,225
Are you okay?

578
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,895
What was that? Really now.

579
00:19:48,478 --> 00:19:50,647
It seems like you did that on purpose.

580
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:51,356
Oka: No.

581
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,733
I didn't know that…

582
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:53,984
you were on your way out.

583
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:54,818
No. I'm really sorry, bro.

584
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:56,528
That was such a strong… push.

585
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:57,279
Atoy: That's enough.

586
00:19:57,362 --> 00:19:58,906
It wasn't on purpose.

587
00:19:58,989 --> 00:19:59,990
Oka: Sorry.

588
00:20:01,116 --> 00:20:03,702
Buddy, please bear with him, okay.

589
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:04,578
Bear with him?

590
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:05,746
I'm the one who should ask for patience.

591
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:06,663
Wow, really.

592
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:07,789
Atoy: No, it's fine now.

593
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:08,749
Come on, come on. Let's go.

594
00:20:08,832 --> 00:20:11,335
Emerson: This guy, sometimes it seems
like he's really trying to ruin things.

595
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:13,212
It’s all in your head.

596
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,546
[tense music playing]

597
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:35,275
[water pouring]

598
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:35,984
Oka.

599
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:36,568
Mmm?

600
00:20:37,527 --> 00:20:38,153
Hi.

601
00:20:39,112 --> 00:20:40,072
Are you okay now?
[closes]

602
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:42,324
I'm okay.

603
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:43,533
Ah, why?

604
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:46,036
No, because…

605
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:48,789
you’re speculating that Atoy
has another woman?

606
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,208
You even followed him.

607
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:53,627
[suspicious music playing]

608
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:57,965
Actually, I even tried to open his phone.

609
00:20:58,048 --> 00:20:58,590
Hmm?

610
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:00,968
But I couldn't guess the password.

611
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:06,431
Then, I felt guilty.

612
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:08,183
I thought…

613
00:21:09,851 --> 00:21:10,936
why am I even doing this?

614
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:12,771
[music continues]

615
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:14,439
Do I not trust my husband?

616
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:18,318
You know, I even found a

617
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:20,320
hair clip in his car.

618
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:23,407
It's difficult, Oka.

619
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:25,450
But maybe

620
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,286
there's a good explanation once
we get to the bottom of it, right?

621
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:30,163
Because, Audrey, I know Atoy.

622
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,541
He's not the type of man

623
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:34,209
who would have a mistress.

624
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:37,379
[music continues]

625
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:44,386
[thuds]
Oh, sorry.

626
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:46,596
Wait, let me clean that.

627
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,724
[heavy music playing]

628
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:57,482
What is that?

629
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:59,776
No, nothing. It's nothing.

630
00:22:01,069 --> 00:22:01,820
Huh?

631
00:22:02,612 --> 00:22:03,780
Let me see.

632
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:04,906
No, no, Audrey. It’s nothing.

633
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:05,657
It's nothing, nothing.

634
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:07,117
Why don't you want to show me?

635
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:08,618
No, it's just trash.

636
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:09,703
So, it'd be a waste if--

637
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:10,454
Wh-- what for?

638
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:12,289
It’s just trash.

639
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:14,624
Audrey.

640
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:15,792
What is this?

641
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:20,672
[tense music playing]

642
00:22:27,429 --> 00:22:32,225
[electronic blipping]

643
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:37,981
[intense music playing]

644
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:39,608
What's our new information

645
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:41,026
about Indigo Resort?

646
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:42,903
On the date Baker gave,

647
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:45,489
there's a private event

648
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:48,366
at the beach resort, a wedding.

649
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:50,202
That means there's…

650
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:51,578
there should be an invitation for that.

651
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:52,621
How will we get in?

652
00:22:52,704 --> 00:22:54,247
Uno, our disguises,

653
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:56,333
Did you tell your wife where you're going?

654
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:58,502
I have eyes on Atoy Padua.

655
00:22:58,585 --> 00:23:00,003
Okay. Here's what you'll do, okay.

656
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:02,464
Don't take your eyes off Atoy.

657
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:03,590
Elias: Do we understand each other?

658
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:04,716
Georgia: Copy, Sir.

659
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,550
Paldo: Oh my god!

660
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:06,843
Is what I'm seeing right?

661
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:09,513
A goddess has arrived here in Tabang Lupa!

662
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:11,681
Audrey: Atoy!

663
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:13,308
[theme music playing]

664
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:15,018
Who is this woman?

665
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,353
And why are you hugging?

666
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,438
Did you deliberately give that to her?

667
00:23:18,522 --> 00:23:20,398
Why would I do that to you, 'Toy?

668
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:21,942
I didn't even know the pic was missing.

669
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:23,652
I'm only realizing it now.

670
00:23:23,735 --> 00:23:25,445
Could it be that you took the picture?

671
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:27,989
♪ If the cutter, knows how to hit ♪
